1:<!doctype html><html lang="en" data-base="" data-news-api=""><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"><title>Where to Eat and Rest in Takua Pa · Takua Pa 101</title><meta name="description" content="Restaurants, cafes and snack stops in Takua Pa that the guide author has visited, with real opening hours and map links, plus a printable walking leaflet."><meta name="robots" content="index,follow,max-image-preview:large"><meta property="og:title" content="Where to Eat and Rest in Takua Pa"><meta property="og:description" content="Restaurants, cafes and snack stops in Takua Pa that the guide author has visited, with real opening hours and map links, plus a printable walking leaflet."><meta property="og:url" content="https://takuapa101.com/rest/"><meta property="og:type" content="website"><meta property="og:image" content="https://takuapa101.com/assets/og/default.png"><meta property="og:locale" content="en_US"><meta property="og:site_name" content="ตะกั่วป่า 101"><meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image"><meta name="twitter:image" content="https://takuapa101.com/assets/og/default.png"><meta name="generator" content="ตะกั่วป่า 101"><link rel="canonical" href="https://takuapa101.com/en/rest/"><link rel="preload" href="/assets/NotoSerifThai.woff2" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin><link rel="preload" href="/assets/IBMPlexSansThaiLooped-Regular.woff2" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/design.css"><script type="application/ld+json">[{"@context": "https://schema.org", "inLanguage": "en", "@type": "BreadcrumbList", "itemListElement": [{"@type": "ListItem", "position": 1, "name": "Home", "item": "https://takuapa101.com/"}, {"@type": "ListItem", "position": 2, "name": "Takua Pa food, cafés, and places to stop", "item": "https://takuapa101.com/rest/"}]}]</script><script src="/assets/design.js" defer></script><script src="/assets/trip.js" defer></script><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/ui.css"><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/theme.css"><script src="/assets/theme.js"></script><script src="/assets/search.js" defer></script><script src="/assets/live-news.js" defer></script><meta name="theme-color" content="#203f39"><link rel="icon" href="/assets/favicon.svg" type="image/svg+xml"><link rel="alternate" hreflang="th" href="https://takuapa101.com/rest/"><link rel="alternate" hreflang="en" href="https://takuapa101.com/en/rest/"><link rel="alternate" hreflang="x-default" href="https://takuapa101.com/rest/"></head><body class="inner-page"><a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to content</a><header class="site-header"><a class="brand" href="/en/" aria-label="ตะกั่วป่า 101 หน้าแรก"><span class="brand-mark">101</span><span>Takua Pa<small>TAKUA PA FIELD NOTES</small></span></a><nav id="main-nav" aria-label="เมนูหลัก"><a href="/en/places/">Places</a><a href="/en/stories/">Stories</a><a href="/en/map/">Map</a><a href="/en/rest/" aria-current="page">Eat and explore</a><a href="/en/news/">Updates</a><a href="/en/trip/">Your trip</a><a href="/en/traditions/" class="nav-more">Traditions</a><a href="/en/eat/" class="nav-more">Eat & Souvenirs</a><a href="/en/routes/" class="nav-more">Walking Routes</a><a href="/en/leaflet/" class="nav-more">Leaflet</a><a href="/en/about/" class="nav-more">About</a></nav><div class="header-tools"><a class="lang-switch" href="/rest/" hreflang="th" lang="th">ไทย</a><button class="theme-toggle" type="button" data-theme-toggle aria-pressed="false" aria-label="สลับเป็นโหมดกลางคืน"><span class="tt-night" aria-hidden="true">☾</span><span class="tt-day" aria-hidden="true">☀</span></button><button class="nav-toggle" type="button" data-nav-toggle aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="main-nav" aria-label="เปิดเมนู"><span class="ib-glyph" aria-hidden="true">☰</span></button><button class="icon-button" type="button" data-open-search aria-label="ค้นหาในเว็บไซต์ (กด Ctrl+K)"><span class="ib-glyph" aria-hidden="true">⌕</span></button><a class="icon-button" href="/en/trip/" aria-label="ทริปของคุณ"><span class="ib-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◫</span><span class="qs-badge" data-trip-count hidden>0</span></a><a class="header-map" href="/en/map/">Open map ↗</a></div></header><main id="main"><div class="intro"><a class="eyebrow" href="/en/">Takua Pa 101 / Old Town Guide</a><h1>Take a break, eat and explore Takuapa</h1><p class="lead">Shops and stops personally visited by the people who made this guide, with opening hours and directions</p></div><p>The whole old town is walkable, but there is little shade and the afternoon sun is strong. Stops along the way make it easier to cover the area.</p><p class="small">The list below is selected from<a href="https://siwaracafe.com/guide" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Siwara Cafe's Takua Pa food and travel guide</a> The people who made this website · Unlike the list of shops on<a href="/en/eat/">the Food and Souvenirs page</a> Every shop listed here has been visited in person, so the opening hours and coordinates are practical and current · Even so, small shops can change their hours at any time, so call ahead before making a long trip.</p><h2>Restaurants and food</h2><div class="rest-stops"><article class="rest-stop pick"><a class="pick-art" href="https://maps.google.com/?q=Baan%20Lapp%20%E0%B8%95%E0%B8%B0%E0%B8%81%E0%B8%B1%E0%B9%88%E0%B8%A7%E0%B8%9B%E0%B9%88%E0%B8%B2" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><img src="/assets/guide/guide-baan-lapp.webp" alt="BAAN LAPP บ้านลัพพ์ (โฮมมี่ &amp; สเต๊ก ตะกั่วป่า)" width="1200" height="1600" loading="lazy"></a><div class="pick-body"><h3>BAAN LAPP (Homey &amp; Steak, Takua Pa)</h3><p>A warm, homey restaurant and cafe with a Hidden Gem style, serving steak, pasta, and carefully prepared fusion dishes.</p><p class="pick-meta">Open 11:00 - 21:00 (closed Wednesdays) · ~2.2 km from Siwara</p><p class="pick-tip">From 17:30 onward, the lights create a pleasant atmosphere. It is suitable for a family dinner.</p><a class="shop-nav" href="https://maps.google.com/?q=Baan%20Lapp%20%E0%B8%95%E0%B8%B0%E0%B8%81%E0%B8%B1%E0%B9%88%E0%B8%A7%E0%B8%9B%E0%B9%88%E0%B8%B2" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Navigate ↗</a></div></article><article class="rest-stop pick"><a class="pick-art" href="https://maps.google.com/?q=%E0%B8%AB%E0%B8%A1%E0%B8%B9%E0%B8%AA%E0%B8%B0%E0%B9%80%E0%B8%95%E0%B9%8A%E0%B8%B0%E0%B8%84%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%B9%E0%B9%81%E0%B8%AD%E0%B9%8B%E0%B8%A7" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><img src="/assets/guide/guide-moo-satay-kruaew.webp" alt="ขนมจีนหมูสะเต๊ะครูแอ๋ว (ทุ่งพระโพธิ์)" width="1590" height="1600" loading="lazy"></a><div class="pick-body"><h3>Kru Aew's Khanom Chin and Pork Satay (Thung Phra Pho)</h3><p>A tucked-away shop in Thung Phra Pho serving tender, juicy charcoal-grilled pork satay marinated with spices, hot off the grill with boldly flavored southern Thai khanom chin and curry.</p><p class="pick-meta">Open 12:00 - 18:00 (closed Thursdays) · ~2.4 km from Siwara</p><p class="pick-tip">The pork satay is grilled fresh, skewer by skewer. A large set of 20 to 30 skewers is recommended with the khanom chin.</p><a class="shop-nav" href="https://maps.google.com/?q=%E0%B8%AB%E0%B8%A1%E0%B8%B9%E0%B8%AA%E0%B8%B0%E0%B9%80%E0%B8%95%E0%B9%8A%E0%B8%B0%E0%B8%84%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%B9%E0%B9%81%E0%B8%AD%E0%B9%8B%E0%B8%A7" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Navigate ↗</a></div></article><article class="rest-stop pick"><a class="pick-art" href="https://maps.google.com/?q=%E0%B8%9A%E0%B8%B0%E0%B8%AB%E0%B8%A1%E0%B8%B5%E0%B9%88%E0%B8%95%E0%B8%A5%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%94%E0%B8%82%E0%B8%A7%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%87" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><img src="/assets/guide/guide-mee-talad-khwang.webp" alt="บะหมี่พังงา ตลาดขวาง" width="1024" height="683" loading="lazy"></a><div class="pick-body"><h3>Phang Nga Noodles, Khwang Market</h3><p>Springy, tender handmade egg noodles made with an old Hokkien recipe, tossed with fragrant fried garlic oil and large pieces of crispy pork lard, for a balanced, mellow flavor.</p><p class="pick-meta">Open 09:00 - 15:30 (closed Tuesdays) · ~0.6 km from Siwara</p><p class="pick-tip">Try the "special dry tom yum noodles with crispy pork lard". Toss well and enjoy without adding seasoning.</p><a class="shop-nav" href="https://maps.google.com/?q=%E0%B8%9A%E0%B8%B0%E0%B8%AB%E0%B8%A1%E0%B8%B5%E0%B9%88%E0%B8%95%E0%B8%A5%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%94%E0%B8%82%E0%B8%A7%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%87" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Navigate ↗</a></div></article><article class="rest-stop pick"><a class="pick-art" href="https://maps.google.com/?q=%E0%B8%9B%E0%B9%89%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%94%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%AB%E0%B8%A1%E0%B8%B5%E0%B9%88%E0%B8%AE%E0%B8%81%E0%B9%80%E0%B8%81%E0%B8%B5%E0%B9%89%E0%B8%A2%E0%B8%99" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><img src="/assets/guide/guide-pa-da-hokkien.webp" alt="ป้าดา หมี่ฮกเกี้ยน (ถนนศรีตะกั่วป่า)" width="1600" height="1600" loading="lazy"></a><div class="pick-body"><h3>Pa Da Hokkien Noodles (Thanon Si Takua Pa)</h3><p>A long-running Hokkien noodle shop on Thanon Si Takua Pa. The springy noodles are stir-fried with a fragrant wok-charred aroma, plenty of seafood, and a runny egg.</p><p class="pick-meta">Open 07:00 - 17:00 (daily) · ~0.7 km from Siwara</p><p class="pick-tip">Try the "Hokkien noodles stir-fried with a runny egg". Break the yolk and mix it into the hot noodles for a rich, savory taste.</p><a class="shop-nav" href="https://maps.google.com/?q=%E0%B8%9B%E0%B9%89%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%94%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%AB%E0%B8%A1%E0%B8%B5%E0%B9%88%E0%B8%AE%E0%B8%81%E0%B9%80%E0%B8%81%E0%B8%B5%E0%B9%89%E0%B8%A2%E0%B8%99" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Navigate ↗</a></div></article><article class="rest-stop pick"><a class="pick-art" href="https://maps.google.com/?q=%E0%B8%A3%E0%B9%89%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%9A%E0%B8%B1%E0%B8%87%E0%B8%94%E0%B8%B5%E0%B8%99%20%E0%B8%95%E0%B8%B0%E0%B8%81%E0%B8%B1%E0%B9%88%E0%B8%A7%E0%B8%9B%E0%B9%88%E0%B8%B2" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><img src="/assets/guide/guide-bang-deen.webp" alt="ร้านบังดีน ข้าวหมกไก่ &amp; โรตีแกง (Michelin Guide)" width="1200" height="1600" loading="lazy"></a><div class="pick-body"><h3>Bangdeen Chicken Biryani &amp; Curry Roti (Michelin Guide)</h3><p>A well-known Muslim breakfast restaurant recognized by the Michelin Guide. Fragrant, tender spiced chicken biryani is served with a bold dipping sauce, along with soft roti and chicken massaman curry.</p><p class="pick-meta">Open 06:00 - 13:30 (daily) · ~2.8 km from Siwara</p><p class="pick-tip">The roti dough is freshly kneaded and fried until crisp yet soft. Try the massaman curry roti with hot pulled tea.</p><a class="shop-nav" href="https://maps.google.com/?q=%E0%B8%A3%E0%B9%89%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%9A%E0%B8%B1%E0%B8%87%E0%B8%94%E0%B8%B5%E0%B8%99%20%E0%B8%95%E0%B8%B0%E0%B8%81%E0%B8%B1%E0%B9%88%E0%B8%A7%E0%B8%9B%E0%B9%88%E0%B8%B2" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Navigate ↗</a></div></article><article class="rest-stop pick"><a class="pick-art" href="https://maps.google.com/?q=%E0%B8%A3%E0%B9%89%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%9B%E0%B8%B9%E0%B8%94%E0%B8%B3%20%E0%B8%9A%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%87%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A2%E0%B8%AA%E0%B8%B5" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><img src="/assets/guide/guide-pu-dam.webp" alt="ร้านปูดำ (บางนายสี)" width="1010" height="761" loading="lazy"></a><div class="pick-body"><h3>Black Crab Restaurant (Bang Nai Si)</h3><p>A tucked-away restaurant beside a mangrove canal in Bang Nai Si, serving fresh wild black crab with firm, intensely sweet meat and boldly seasoned local-style dishes.</p><p class="pick-meta">Open 10:00 - 21:00 (daily) · ~3.2 km from Siwara</p><p class="pick-tip">Steamed black crab and crab fried rice are the most frequently ordered dishes. Call ahead to check fresh supplies or go before evening.</p><a class="shop-nav" href="https://maps.google.com/?q=%E0%B8%A3%E0%B9%89%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%9B%E0%B8%B9%E0%B8%94%E0%B8%B3%20%E0%B8%9A%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%87%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A2%E0%B8%AA%E0%B8%B5" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Navigate ↗</a></div></article><article class="rest-stop pick"><a class="pick-art" href="https://maps.google.com/?q=%E0%B9%80%E0%B8%81%E0%B9%8B%E0%B8%9C%E0%B8%B1%E0%B8%94%E0%B9%84%E0%B8%97%E0%B8%A2%20%E0%B8%95%E0%B8%B0%E0%B8%81%E0%B8%B1%E0%B9%88%E0%B8%A7%E0%B8%9B%E0%B9%88%E0%B8%B2" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><img src="/assets/guide/guide-kae-padthai.webp" alt="เก๋ ผัดไทย (ตลาดเก่าตะกั่วป่า)" width="1131" height="1600" loading="lazy"></a><div class="pick-body"><h3>Kae Pad Thai (Takua Pa Old Market)</h3><p>A popular Pad Thai shop in the old town area. Chewy noodles stir-fried in a rich traditional tamarind sauce, with large, fresh, and bouncy shrimp.</p><p class="pick-meta">Open 16:30 to 21:30 (daily) · ~0.6 km from Siwara</p><p class="pick-tip">Fresh shrimp Pad Thai wrapped in egg is the specialty. Squeeze fresh lime over it and eat with banana blossom and pennywort. Flavorful without extra seasoning.</p><a class="shop-nav" href="https://maps.google.com/?q=%E0%B9%80%E0%B8%81%E0%B9%8B%E0%B8%9C%E0%B8%B1%E0%B8%94%E0%B9%84%E0%B8%97%E0%B8%A2%20%E0%B8%95%E0%B8%B0%E0%B8%81%E0%B8%B1%E0%B9%88%E0%B8%A7%E0%B8%9B%E0%B9%88%E0%B8%B2" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Navigate ↗</a></div></article><article class="rest-stop pick"><a class="pick-art" href="https://maps.google.com/?q=%E0%B9%80%E0%B8%88%E0%B9%8A%E0%B8%AD%E0%B9%89%E0%B8%A7%E0%B8%99%20%E0%B8%9A%E0%B9%89%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%99%E0%B9%89%E0%B8%B3%E0%B9%80%E0%B8%84%E0%B9%87%E0%B8%A1" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><img src="/assets/guide/guide-jae-ouan.webp" alt="เจ๊อ้วน ทะเลสด (บ้านน้ำเค็ม)" width="1200" height="1600" loading="lazy"></a><div class="pick-body"><h3>Jae Uan Talay Sod (Baan Nam Kem)</h3><p>A renowned seafood restaurant in the Baan Nam Kem area. Fresh ingredients delivered directly from fishing boats daily. Spicy seafood dip made with real lime. Evening seaside atmosphere.</p><p class="pick-meta">Hours: 10:30 to 21:30 (Daily) · ~11.5 km from Siwara</p><p class="pick-tip">Great for dinner. Large tiger prawns with firm, sweet meat paired with spicy seafood dip.</p><a class="shop-nav" href="https://maps.google.com/?q=%E0%B9%80%E0%B8%88%E0%B9%8A%E0%B8%AD%E0%B9%89%E0%B8%A7%E0%B8%99%20%E0%B8%9A%E0%B9%89%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%99%E0%B9%89%E0%B8%B3%E0%B9%80%E0%B8%84%E0%B9%87%E0%B8%A1" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Navigate ↗</a></div></article></div><h2>Stops and Attractions</h2><div class="rest-stops"><article class="rest-stop pick"><a class="pick-art" href="https://maps.google.com/?q=%E0%B8%96%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%A8%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%B5%E0%B8%95%E0%B8%B0%E0%B8%81%E0%B8%B1%E0%B9%88%E0%B8%A7%E0%B8%9B%E0%B9%88%E0%B8%B2" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><img src="/assets/guide/guide-old-town-street.webp" alt="ถนนวัฒนธรรมศรีตะกั่วป่า &amp; สตรีทอาร์ตตึกโบราณ" width="1200" height="800" loading="lazy"></a><div class="pick-body"><h3>Thanon Si Takua Pa &amp; Old Building Street Art</h3><p>An old shophouse district with arched walkways (Five-Foot Way) featuring street art that tells the stories of the Baba people and the town's tin mining history.</p><p class="pick-meta">Hours: Open all day (09:00 to 17:00 recommended) · ~0.7 km from Siwara</p><p class="pick-tip">You can easily walk through various alleys connecting to Tao Sor pastry shops and old town eateries.</p><a class="shop-nav" href="https://maps.google.com/?q=%E0%B8%96%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%A8%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%B5%E0%B8%95%E0%B8%B0%E0%B8%81%E0%B8%B1%E0%B9%88%E0%B8%A7%E0%B8%9B%E0%B9%88%E0%B8%B2" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Navigate ↗</a></div></article><article class="rest-stop pick"><a class="pick-art" href="https://maps.google.com/?q=%E0%B8%99%E0%B9%89%E0%B8%B3%E0%B8%95%E0%B8%81%E0%B8%95%E0%B8%B3%E0%B8%AB%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%B1%E0%B8%87" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><img src="/assets/guide/guide-tam-nang.webp" alt="น้ำตกตำหนัง (อุทยานแห่งชาติศรีพังงา)" width="1600" height="1060" loading="lazy"></a><div class="pick-body"><h3>Tam Nang Waterfall (Si Phang Nga National Park)</h3><p>A large waterfall in the middle of a lush rainforest in Si Phang-nga National Park. The water cascades down a 63-meter high cliff into a clear pool where Mahseer barbs swim.</p><p class="pick-meta">Hours: 08:30 to 16:30 (Daily) · ~21.8 km from Siwara</p><p class="pick-tip">Between 10:00 and 14:00, the sunlight hits the water surface beautifully. There is a shaded resting spot under large trees.</p><a class="shop-nav" href="https://maps.google.com/?q=%E0%B8%99%E0%B9%89%E0%B8%B3%E0%B8%95%E0%B8%81%E0%B8%95%E0%B8%B3%E0%B8%AB%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%B1%E0%B8%87" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Navigate ↗</a></div></article><article class="rest-stop pick"><a class="pick-art" href="https://maps.google.com/?q=%E0%B8%AA%E0%B8%B0%E0%B8%9E%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%99%E0%B9%80%E0%B8%AB%E0%B8%A5%E0%B9%87%E0%B8%81%20%E0%B8%95%E0%B8%B0%E0%B8%81%E0%B8%B1%E0%B9%88%E0%B8%A7%E0%B8%9B%E0%B9%88%E0%B8%B2" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><img src="/assets/guide/guide-iron-bridge.webp" alt="สะพานเหล็กบุญสูง (สะพานโคกขนุน)" width="1600" height="1200" loading="lazy"></a><div class="pick-body"><h3>Boonsung Iron Bridge (Khok Khanun Bridge)</h3><p>A historical landmark from the prosperous tin mining era. Built from the steel parts of an old tin dredger, elegantly spanning the Takua Pa River.</p><p class="pick-meta">Hours: Open 24 hours (16:30 to 18:30 recommended) · ~2.3 km from Siwara</p><p class="pick-tip">Between 17:00 and 18:30, the sunset light shines through the steel bridge structure, turning it into a beautiful orange. Great for taking photos.</p><a class="shop-nav" href="https://maps.google.com/?q=%E0%B8%AA%E0%B8%B0%E0%B8%9E%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%99%E0%B9%80%E0%B8%AB%E0%B8%A5%E0%B9%87%E0%B8%81%20%E0%B8%95%E0%B8%B0%E0%B8%81%E0%B8%B1%E0%B9%88%E0%B8%A7%E0%B8%9B%E0%B9%88%E0%B8%B2" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Navigate ↗</a></div></article><article class="rest-stop pick"><a class="pick-art" href="https://maps.google.com/?q=%E0%B8%AB%E0%B8%A5%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%94%E0%B9%83%E0%B8%AB%E0%B8%8D%E0%B9%88%20%E0%B8%95%E0%B8%B0%E0%B8%81%E0%B8%B1%E0%B9%88%E0%B8%A7%E0%B8%9B%E0%B9%88%E0%B8%B2" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><img src="/assets/guide/guide-lad-yai.webp" alt="หลาดใหญ่ ถนนคนเดินสายวัฒนธรรมเมืองเก่า" width="1600" height="1066" loading="lazy"></a><div class="pick-body"><h3>Lad Yai, the old town cultural walking street</h3><p>A classic historical walking street. Thanon Si Takua Pa is closed to traffic so locals can set up stalls selling traditional food, local snacks, and crafts under Sino-Portuguese style lighting.</p><p class="pick-meta">Hours: Sundays only 15:30 to 20:30 · ~0.7 km from Siwara</p><p class="pick-tip">Open only on Sundays. Arriving around 17:00 is recommended when the orange sunlight beautifully lights up the classic old buildings for photos.</p><a class="shop-nav" href="https://maps.google.com/?q=%E0%B8%AB%E0%B8%A5%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%94%E0%B9%83%E0%B8%AB%E0%B8%8D%E0%B9%88%20%E0%B8%95%E0%B8%B0%E0%B8%81%E0%B8%B1%E0%B9%88%E0%B8%A7%E0%B8%9B%E0%B9%88%E0%B8%B2" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Navigate ↗</a></div></article></div><h2>Souvenirs</h2><div class="rest-stops"><article class="rest-stop pick"><a class="pick-art" href="https://maps.google.com/?q=%E0%B9%80%E0%B8%95%E0%B9%89%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%AA%E0%B9%89%E0%B8%AD%E0%B8%95%E0%B8%A7%E0%B8%87%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%B1%E0%B8%95%E0%B8%99%E0%B9%8C" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><img src="/assets/guide/guide-tuangrat-taosor.webp" alt="เต้าส้อตวงรัตน์ (ต้นตำรับ 100 ปี)" width="1600" height="1200" loading="lazy"></a><div class="pick-body"><h3>Tao Sor Tuang Rat (100-year-old original recipe)</h3><p>A top souvenir of Takua Pa. Thin crispy crust with dense mung bean filling, scented with traditional candle smoke. The recipe has been passed down through generations.</p><p class="pick-meta">Hours: 08:00 to 17:00 (Daily) · ~0.6 km from Siwara</p><p class="pick-tip">The salted egg yolk filling is their signature. Best bought fresh out of the oven. Can be kept for 7 to 10 days.</p><a class="shop-nav" href="https://maps.google.com/?q=%E0%B9%80%E0%B8%95%E0%B9%89%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%AA%E0%B9%89%E0%B8%AD%E0%B8%95%E0%B8%A7%E0%B8%87%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%B1%E0%B8%95%E0%B8%99%E0%B9%8C" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Navigate ↗</a></div></article></div><h2>Walking Pamphlet</h2><div class="leaflet-block"><a class="leaflet-art" href="/assets/leaflet/takuapa-walk-leaflet.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><img src="/assets/leaflet/leaflet-page-1.webp" alt="แผ่นพับเดินเมืองเก่าตะกั่วป่า หน้าแรก" width="1400" height="990" loading="lazy"></a><div class="leaflet-copy"><p>A two-page pamphlet detailing the wooden house and four stops on the route above. Print on A4 paper, fold in half, and carry it with you. No need to look at your phone in the sun.</p><div class="leaflet-actions"><a class="button" href="/assets/leaflet/takuapa-walk-leaflet.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">โหลดแผ่นพับ PDF · 7.6 MB</a><a class="text-link" href="/en/leaflet/">Read on the website instead ↗</a></div><p class="small">Created by<a href="https://siwaracafe.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Siwara Cafe</a> Creators of this guide · Free to distribute and print</p></div></div>
2:    <h2>The Wooden House Behind This Guide</h2>
4:        <p>This website is created by Siwara Cafe, a teak house with wooden gables, stained glass, and old doors, located at 53 Thanon Rat Bamrung in the old market area.</p>
5:        <a href="https://siwaracafe.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Get to know Siwara House, the guide creator ↗</a>
7:    <h2>Short Walking Route from the Wooden House</h2><div class="short-walk"><article class="walk-point"><a href="/en/places/khun-in/"><img src="/assets/khun-in.webp" alt="บ้านขุนอินทร์" width="1000" height="1000" loading="lazy"></a><div><h3><a href="/en/places/khun-in/">Khun In House</a></h3><p>Notice: Porch Roof and Openings</p><button data-trip-add="khun-in">Add to trip</button></div></article><article class="walk-point"><a href="/en/places/tao-ming/"><img src="/assets/tao-ming.webp" alt="โรงเรียนเต้าหมิง" width="1000" height="667" loading="lazy"></a><div><h3><a href="/en/places/tao-ming/">Tao Ming School</a></h3><p>Notice: Gable and Yellow Balcony</p><button data-trip-add="tao-ming">Add to trip</button></div></article><article class="walk-point"><a href="/en/places/guan-yu/"><img src="/assets/guan-yu.webp" alt="ศาลเจ้าพ่อกวนอู ซิ่นไช่ตึ๋ง" width="1000" height="1000" loading="lazy"></a><div><h3><a href="/en/places/guan-yu/">Guan Yu / Sin Chai Tung Shrine</a></h3><p>Notice: Door and Red Details</p><button data-trip-add="guan-yu">Add to trip</button></div></article><article class="walk-point"><a href="/en/places/iron-bridge/"><img src="/assets/iron-bridge.webp" alt="สะพานเหล็กบุญสูง" width="1000" height="1000" loading="lazy"></a><div><h3><a href="/en/places/iron-bridge/">Boon Soong Iron Bridge</a></h3><p>Notice: Steel Structure and Riverside Landscape</p><button data-trip-add="iron-bridge">Add to trip</button></div></article></div><p>Plan further: <a href="/en/trip/">Plan your trip ↗</a> · <a href="/en/map/">View town map ↗</a></p><aside class="source"><h2>Data Sources</h2><p>Compiled from<a href="https://www.takuapacity.go.th/pdf/travel-preview.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Takua Pa Town Municipality brochure</a> · Data extracted September 6, 2026 (2569 BE). The document does not specify a publication date. Opening hours, shop status, and current schedules are not verified. Please check with the venue before traveling.</p></aside><script type="application