FAQ
Getting there from Takua Pa Town
Located in the Takua Pa old town community on Si Takua Pa Road; use a navigation map to the specified coordinates.
What is the history of this place?
The building was constructed in 1922 (2465 BE). The school started requesting to be established as a private school in 1920 (2463 BE) and originally used the name To Beng according to the Hokkien accent.
What are the highlights to see?
A historical school building remaining in the old town area. Observe the building shape and corrugated zinc roof identified by conservation agencies. It is evidence of educational management by the Chinese community in the tin mining town of Takua Pa.
