เส้นเวลา เลื่อนเพื่ออ่านเหตุการณ์
Application for Toh Beng Private School
The Chinese school, initially operated informally by private individuals, applied for private school status following the Private Schools Act of 1918.
Construction of Tao Ming School Building
The applied Sino-Portuguese building was constructed with donations from tin mining tycoons and Chinese merchants to provide primary and Chinese language education for children in Takua Pa.
Local sources state that tin mines began to gradually close during this decade, reducing the town's vibrancy. However, this is not a verified year for the school's closure.
Municipality Releases Promotional Video
Takua Pa Municipality published a video introducing the Tao Ming School building as an old town tourist attraction.
Old Town Storytelling Event at Tao Ming School
Press releases indicated the Old Town Storytelling event took place at Tao Ming School, Takua Pa. However, full details from primary news sources are not verified.
School Closes and Foundation Takes Over
The exact year of closure is not verified. Official sources state the remaining building is under the care of the Tao Ming Takua Pa School Foundation.
